**Definition 5.4 (bounded source locator).** Initialize the canonical
represented entrance/reservoir from this immutable cover, not from current
source16. Clear tally, entry/exit flags and saved endpoints. Copy the
actual constructed $1^b$ to rem. While rem is nonempty, perform the
following finite word operations in written order.

1. Decode only the represented physical control/version/PC and its next
   actual row; compare with the fixed entry/exit sets and the retained
   unary $j$. Save these two finite test results in word fields before
   Step reuses its temporaries. An exit without a saved entry, or another
   qualifying entry after the first, is binding failure.
2. Execute exactly one Step on that state/reservoir. If it returns a
   simulated failure, take description/dependency/binding failure according
   to its first failing check. Otherwise the new tally is the successor
   tally. Tail rem once.
3. On the saved entry test copy this successor tally to $e$ and set the
   entry flag. On the saved exit test copy it to $f$ and terminate the
   locator successfully. These are compiled bank copies and flag writes.

If rem empties without both endpoints, return NoOccurrence. The search
never executes a represented row after $b$; unsuccessful search cannot
wait for a source call that might occur later. On success cancel $e$
from $f$, require $t\le f-e$, construct $1^k$ by Cat of $1^e,1^t$,
and require $a\le e\le k\le f\le b$. Emit $U(k)$ separately.
Set start=$e$, end=$f$, anchor-kind=1 and anchor to the exact four-field
tuple $(m,j,\text{unified-row origin},\text{complete request origins})$.
The origins identify this already completed occurrence now; their later
delivery is not asserted at its older entry or selected cut.

